// expect: compile_error
// expect-error: E486
// Expected: E486 Underivable Class
//   "`Eq` cannot be derived for `Pair`, which has more than one type
//    parameter. Write the instance by hand."
//
// Proposal 0179. A head with one type parameter derives fine — see
// `examples/type_classes/derived_parameterized_eq.flx`. Two parameters give
// the instance two context constraints of the same class, and the generated
// body compares fields bound by a `case` pattern. Core's dictionary selection
// picks between same-class dictionaries by the argument's type, which a
// pattern binder does not carry, so every field resolves through the first
// dictionary and the second parameter is compared with the wrong evidence.
//
// Rejecting the clause makes that a diagnostic rather than a wrong answer; a
// hand-written instance is unaffected.

data Pair<a, b> { Pair(a, b) } deriving (Eq)

fn main() with IO {
    print(1)
}
